%% PACT v1.0 — informative diagram for section 4.
%% Logical responsibilities and information exchange, not message order.
%% Roles may be colocated. Evidence arrows do not require direct network calls.
%% Execution requires valid native authentication, ADMISSIBLE PACT admission,
%% current native authorization, and all native execution conditions.
flowchart TB
    accTitle: PACT control and data boundaries
    accDescr: The gateway combines PACT admission with native authentication, authorization, and execution checks. External approval evidence can satisfy applicable requirements, while authorized exceptions remain governed by native policy.

    A["Agent"]

    subgraph ENV["Existing controlled environment"]
        G["Gateway and enforcement"]
        N["Native identity and authorization"]
        R["Protected resource"]
    end

    subgraph PACT["PACT logical roles"]
        Q["Requirement publisher"]
        V["PACT validator"]
    end

    E["Trusted evidence and reputation sources"]
    H["External approval system"]

    A -->|Signed presentation and actual request| G
    G -->|Signed requirement contract| A
    Q -->|Base and authorized adaptive requirements| G
    G -->|Presentation and bound native context| V
    E -->|Claims, status, and reputation evidence| V
    H -->|Trusted approval evidence and status| V
    V -->|Admission result and signed receipt| G
    G -->|Principal, action, resource, and approval context| N
    H -->|Approval or exception recognized by native policy| N
    N -->|Identity context and current authorization decision| G
    G -->|All four execution conditions pass| R
